---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Newsletter from '../components/Newsletter.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title={`About — ${SITE_TITLE}`}
      description="Who we are and why we drag a vegan toddler around the world."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main>
      <section class="section">
        <div class="container prose">
        <span class="eyebrow">About us</span>
        <h1>Hi — we're Daniel, Dafna &amp; Luca.</h1>
        <p>
          A vegan family of three from Vienna, traveling around Europe
          with our four-year-old and refusing to accept that having a
          kid means eating at the hotel buffet forever.
        </p>
        <p>
          We keep the flights short — Luca runs on an energy source
          science has yet to classify, and no one on a ten-hour flight
          deserves to share a cabin with it. Europe suits us fine:
          there's more here than we'll ever finish.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our style is what you might call alternative travel. We plan
          around Luca, but we don't disappear into kids-only itineraries:
          the trips still make room for the things we love — the best
          specialty coffee and pastries in town, vegan food worth a
          detour, craft beer, galleries, and electronic music. It turns
          out a four-year-old copes remarkably well with all of the
          above, given enough cardamom buns.
        </p>
        <p>
          Everything on this site is field-tested: every restaurant was
          eaten at, every museum survived, every snack spilled on. No
          press-trip fluff — if a city was hard, we say so.
        </p>
        <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Destination guides for vegan families, city by city</li>
          <li>The best cafés, pastries, and craft beer near the playground</li>
          <li>Galleries, museums, and culture that tolerate a small loud critic</li>
          <li>Honest verdicts: what worked, what didn't, what it cost</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Say hi</h2>
        <p>
          We're not on social media — the newsletter is where to find us.
          Join it below, reply to any email, and we'll read it. You can
          also follow along the old-fashioned way via
          <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a>.
        </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
    <Newsletter />
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
